"<b>Morale</b> is how a fighter feels this week, and it walks out onto the sand with them: <b>80+</b> high spirits (+1 AP, +1 CF when the bout begins, fights bolder) · <b>35-79</b> steady · <b>under 35</b> low (−1 AP, fights cautiously) · <b>under 20</b> broken (also fights a whole tier worse). It rises with bouts, fair wages, meals, kin tickets and bonuses, and falls with idle weeks, low pay and a greedy lanista. Very low morale also invites early retirement and poachers.\n     <b>Loyalty</b> is their bond to your ludus (from your Honor, their morale, minus your Greed, plus the bonds you build). It is the number a rival must beat to poach them, it decides who stays when the legions call, and it keeps contracts renewing.":"<b>Morale</b> is how a fighter feels this week, and it walks out onto the sand with them: <b>80+</b> high spirits (+1 AP, +1 CF when the bout begins, fights bolder) · <b>35-79</b> steady · <b>under 35</b> low (−1 AP, fights cautiously) · <b>under 20</b> broken (also fights a whole tier worse). It rises with bouts, fair wages, meals, kin tickets and bonuses, and falls with idle weeks, low pay and a greedy lanista. Very low morale also invites early retirement and poachers.\n     <b>Loyalty</b> is their bond to your ludus (from your Honour, their morale, minus your Greed, plus the bonds you build). It is the number a rival must beat to poach them, it decides who stays when the legions call, and it keeps contracts renewing.",
