"New in v0.19: <b>🐾 Menagerie</b> — Beasts &amp; cards grown into a full window with a Bestiary: lore, stats and all-time ledgers (slain, gladiators eaten, tamed) for every beast; <b>Imperium reworked</b> — fans now travel real roads and sea lanes (⛵ dashed) instead of crow-flight, the radar sweep is gone, weather reads bolder, a ⚔️ <b>war-map layer</b> shows who presses whom (severity-3 wars CLOSE that arena and the levy may conscript soldiers — survive the war for a hero's return, +rating, +fame, fans across the empire), 🌋 <b>Vesuvius</b> stirs near Pompeii, and the focused city gets its own framed tile; Ludus gladiators wear <b>star ratings</b> everywhere; Manager mode gains a 🏜 <b>Sandbox</b> (lethality, blood-money prices, injuries, training gains, rookie influx — all sliders), a season-ending <b>festival finale</b> in Roma (leader picks the festival, top four stables draft champions, Cassian presides), 🏺 <b>Archives</b> (every Acta of the season re-readable, leather-bound season recaps, also shelved in the Annals), 📯 <b>promotion</b> (feast a city, sponsor games, hire criers — fans land on the Imperium map), 🤝 <b>bout-fixing</b> (guaranteed win, real risk: caught twice in a career and Flavius seizes the ludus; even unseen, bought palms weigh on the barracks), an ⚕ <b>Infirmary</b> (the wound picks its cure — rest, Medicus, or the surgeon's knife; festering wounds kill, send fighters fleeing, or scar them; bathhouse days and the priests of Asclepius for the rich; badly-hurt arena survivors are now carried to the Ludus infirmary automatically and must be treated within four events), tab icons throughout, ★ <b>Favorites</b> (the Board, renamed and explained), a sharper <b>Your scouts</b> column (▲ value / ▼ trap against the bookmaker), hoverable disabled buttons that say what they need, an on-screen 📍 location chip for every event, a hoverable <b>coin ledger</b> on the player board, and smarter CPU tunnels (escape AND travel) and pillar-toppling (weaponless looters bring the pillar down).":"New in v0.19: <b>🐾 Menagerie</b> — Beasts &amp; cards grown into a full window with a Bestiary: lore, stats and all-time ledgers (slain, gladiators eaten, tamed) for every beast; <b>Imperium reworked</b> — fans now travel real roads and sea lanes (⛵ dashed) instead of crow-flight, the radar sweep is gone, weather reads bolder, a ⚔️ <b>war-map layer</b> shows who presses whom (severity-3 wars CLOSE that arena and the levy may conscript soldiers — survive the war for a hero's return, +rating, +fame, fans across the empire), 🌋 <b>Vesuvius</b> stirs near Pompeii, and the focused city gets its own framed tile; Ludus gladiators wear <b>star ratings</b> everywhere; Manager mode gains a 🏜 <b>Sandbox</b> (lethality, blood-money prices, injuries, training gains, rookie influx — all sliders), a season-ending <b>festival finale</b> in Roma (leader picks the festival, top four stables draft champions, Cassian presides), 🏺 <b>Archives</b> (every Acta of the season re-readable, leather-bound season recaps, also shelved in the Annals), 📯 <b>promotion</b> (feast a city, sponsor games, hire criers — fans land on the Imperium map), 🤝 <b>bout-fixing</b> (guaranteed win, real risk: caught twice in a career and Flavius seizes the ludus; even unseen, bought palms weigh on the barracks), an ⚕ <b>Infirmary</b> (the wound picks its cure — rest, Medicus, or the surgeon's knife; festering wounds kill, send fighters fleeing, or scar them; bathhouse days and the priests of Asclepius for the rich; badly-hurt arena survivors are now carried to the Ludus infirmary automatically and must be treated within four events), tab icons throughout, ★ <b>Favourites</b> (the Board, renamed and explained), a sharper <b>Your scouts</b> column (▲ value / ▼ trap against the bookmaker), hoverable disabled buttons that say what they need, an on-screen 📍 location chip for every event, a hoverable <b>coin ledger</b> on the player board, and smarter CPU tunnels (escape AND travel) and pillar-toppling (weaponless looters bring the pillar down).",
"New in v0.20: the empire keeps a <b>calendar</b> — a Roman date on every event, and a 12-week <b>season schedule</b> (one arena a week, classics by far the commonest, rare specials with fatter purses, Cassian's Grand Games in week XII) that Manager mode locks into and New event opens on (play off-schedule if you like); the top bar reads where, when, and the round in one breath; <b>every city names its own beasts</b> (Capua's bears are Tifata and Sannio, its champion Spartacus…) — with per-beast ledgers in the Menagerie, custom beasts' ledgers, and a 🐾 beast tab in the name generator; manager mode: <b>bribe the levy</b> (or let them march), a <b>bookmaker's cut</b> of every wager laid on your rostered fighters, 🔭 <b>arena scouting</b> ahead of match night (+1 AP, +1 coin at the gates), Promote and Schooling moved to Your ludus, and a Lanista tab that fits on one screen; <b>Imperium</b>: the empire's 15 weightiest events up top, then a city card with the stands, local news and mood, the pens, the top-5 local heroes, who lives there and what they are doing right now (attendees only during a live event); spectators wear <b>two-part togas</b> (tunic in their home city's wool, mantle in their fighter's colors); a CF ledger on the player board (hover CF ⓘ); Flavius keeps clear of the sand with the stands off; big windows hold their size across tabs; and Infamis &amp; Hall is now <b>the Annals</b>.":"New in v0.20: the empire keeps a <b>calendar</b> — a Roman date on every event, and a 12-week <b>season schedule</b> (one arena a week, classics by far the commonest, rare specials with fatter purses, Cassian's Grand Games in week XII) that Manager mode locks into and New event opens on (play off-schedule if you like); the top bar reads where, when, and the round in one breath; <b>every city names its own beasts</b> (Capua's bears are Tifata and Sannio, its champion Spartacus…) — with per-beast ledgers in the Menagerie, custom beasts' ledgers, and a 🐾 beast tab in the name generator; manager mode: <b>bribe the levy</b> (or let them march), a <b>bookmaker's cut</b> of every wager laid on your rostered fighters, 🔭 <b>arena scouting</b> ahead of match night (+1 AP, +1 coin at the gates), Promote and Schooling moved to Your ludus, and a Lanista tab that fits on one screen; <b>Imperium</b>: the empire's 15 weightiest events up top, then a city card with the stands, local news and mood, the pens, the top-5 local heroes, who lives there and what they are doing right now (attendees only during a live event); spectators wear <b>two-part togas</b> (tunic in their home city's wool, mantle in their fighter's colours); a CF ledger on the player board (hover CF ⓘ); Flavius keeps clear of the sand with the stands off; big windows hold their size across tabs; and Infamis &amp; Hall is now <b>the Annals</b>.",
